1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Most white belts are just collecting moves.

2
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:06,520
Monday you'll learn to sweep,

3
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:08,000
Wednesday you'll learn a guard pass,

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,360
Friday you'll learn submissions,

5
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:11,280
and your brain is building a giant folder

6
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:12,600
of things you can do.

7
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,680
But none of them connect, all linked together.

8
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:16,120
So when you roll, you're guessing.

9
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:17,240
You know what the move looks like,

10
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:19,840
but you have no idea when it should appear,

11
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:20,920
what reaction set it up,

12
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:22,440
and what position leads into it,

13
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:25,080
and what you're going to do after it does or doesn't work.

14
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:27,120
So you just try something random,

15
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:28,520
and it obviously fails.

16
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:29,600
It turns into a scramble,

17
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:31,280
and then scrambles turn into survival mode.

18
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:32,520
It's not a technique problem,

19
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:33,760
it's a context problem.

20
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:35,720
Moves only work when they leave inside a system,

21
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:38,720
and until your techniques have a system to fit within,

22
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:40,720
you're always just going to be a step behind.

